{
  "analysis": "Inclusion is the bottleneck: 139/179 missed, 78% in the smallest size tertile (recall 0.14), median missed 35px vs 90px train median; round 1's 0.3-0.8 prefer_small on only 6 line sources left recall at 0.27, suggesting pastes were too tiny to learn and source diversity was low. Patches (0.66) and scratches (0.625) are healthier but still miss small/low-contrast instances (low-contrast patch recall 0.28; scratch low-size recall 0.46). Missed crops for all three classes are thin, faint, small streaks/blobs, matching the available source shapes.",
  "allocation": {"inclusion": 30, "patches": 12, "scratches": 8},
  "params": {
    "inclusion": {"scale_min": 0.5, "scale_max": 1.2, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
    "patches": {"scale_min": 0.5, "scale_max": 1.1, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []},
    "scratches": {"scale_min": 0.4, "scale_max": 1.0, "target_pool": "same_class", "source_weighting": "prefer_small", "max_overlap": 0.15, "sources": []}
  },
  "rationale": "Change what failed: drop the sub-0.4 scales that likely produced unlearnable micro-pastes, shift to a learnable small range (0.4-1.2) biased small to target the missed 35-55px instances, and use the full source pool for shape/contrast diversity (inclusion round 1 used only 6 sources). Concentrate the 50-image budget on the worst class (inclusion 30, cumulative 55 < 105 cap) while keeping patches (12) and scratches (8) fed so the shared detector doesn't starve them."
}

The previews match the missed defects well: inclusion pastes are thin, faint, small streaks (matching the missed low-contrast thin lines); patches are realistic dark blobs of varied shape; scratches are thin bright/dark lines at small-to-medium scale. No harsh edges, no wrong-class shapes, no wasted oversized pastes, and the sizes sit in the learnable small range that targets the missed 35–55px instances. Repeating the same plan.

